-- title:
--   Computing the initial graph-sketch matrix over all vertices
-- statement:
--   Given a graph arc list $A$, dimensions $n,k$, and trial signs $\omega$, suppose the native headers and cached-sign bank are ready, the vertex register is zero, the vertex counter has $n$ markers, the wedge depth has $k$ markers, and the stated helpers are empty. The first-vertices loop constructs all initial arrays
--   $$D_1(v,a)=\operatorname{denseLayer}(A,\sigma_\omega,R_\omega,1,v,a)\quad(v<n,\ a<k).$$
--   Their marked frames are prepended to the current bank in reverse vertex and state order. The vertex becomes $n$ and its counter becomes empty; other state and tails are preserved. The time bound is $(\operatorname{firstVertexCost}(n,k)+31)n+30$. This certifies the full initialization layer of the graph recurrence.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/FirstVertices.lean, line 22; source snapshot SHA-256 87a93bbccdbd9dbd3656f1c369d06a8cc732ca81533ee96cfedbc7c6689339f7.

